Varaico OTTO update (tracks varaico, varaicoSuppl on hg19, hg38, hs1)
Contact: Johannes Birgmeier <jbirgmei@ucsc.edu>. Redmine #38543, #38546.

What it does
  doUpdate.sh runs daily from otto's crontab in /hive/data/outside/otto/varaico.
  It installs the newest build staged under /hive/users/jbirgmei/TRACK_VERSIONS/
  whose directory contains a non-empty READY file, unless that build is already
  the one in currentRelease.txt (then it exits quietly, without mail).
  Builds are identified by their build date only; there are no release numbers.

Staging a build (developer side, built by the amelie2 pipeline)
  /hive/users/jbirgmei/TRACK_VERSIONS/<YYYYMMDD>/
      {hg19,hg38,hs1}/normalized_variants.<db>.bb               -> varaico
      {hg19,hg38,hs1}/normalized_variants_supplements.<db>.bb   -> varaicoSuppl
      READY   one line, the version shown on the track page, e.g. "20270301"
  Write READY last, after every file is in place.
  Older dirs are named v<N>_<YYYYMMDD>; the date part is what counts. The newest
  build is the READY dir with the latest date, and it must be newer than the
  installed one.

Checks (before anything changes; any failure mails the log and changes nothing)
  - every bigBed opens (bigBedInfo)
  - item count within +-20% of the installed file
  - every chrom is in /hive/data/genomes/<db>/chrom.sizes
  A refused build stays refused (and mails daily) until it is fixed or a newer
  build is staged. To install an intended big change, do the steps by hand.

Install
  - archive the installed build under its date:
    /hive/data/genomes/<db>/bed/varaico.<date>/<db>.varaico{,Suppl}.<date>.bb,
    linked from htdocs-hgdownload/goldenPath/archive/<db>/varaico/<date>/
    (refuses if that archive file exists with different contents)
  - copy the new files to /hive/data/genomes/<db>/bed/varaico/varaico{,Suppl}.bb
    via a temp file + mv; write varaicoVersion.txt there
  - /gbdb/<db>/bbi/varaico{,Suppl}.bb and varaicoVersion.txt point at those files
    (trackDb: dataVersion /gbdb/$D/bbi/varaicoVersion.txt)
  - mail the log on success
  autoPush (#38546) then copies the /gbdb files to the RR.

Manual use
  ./doUpdate.sh --dry-run    run the checks against the newest READY build only
  Logs: logs/YYYY/MM/*.log
